Experiment No.: 13

Title

Demonstration of SPI Communication Protocol

Aim

To demonstrate SPI communication using Arduino.

Theory

SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface) is a synchronous communication protocol that uses four lines: MOSI, MISO, SCK, and SS for communication between devices.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
SPI Device
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect SPI pins properly.
Include SPI library.
Upload the program.
Observe data transfer.
Code
#include <SPI.h>

void setup()
{
  SPI.begin();
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop()
{
  byte data = SPI.transfer(0x55);

  Serial.println(data);

  delay(1000);
}
Output

SPI data transfer is observed through Serial Monitor.

Result

SPI communication was successfully demonstrated.

Conclusion

The SPI communication protocol was studied successfully.
